{"kind":"article","sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples"]}],"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Design Principles"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingYourFirstApp"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"],"anchor":"Explanation","title":"Explanation","generated":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux’s surface area looks small — a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a reducer protocol, a plugin protocol — but the API is opinionated. These principles explain ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"why","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" the API has the shape it does, so you can extend it correctly."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"1. State is a value, observation is a class","type":"heading","anchor":"1-State-is-a-value-observation-is-a-class"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"State is a struct. Mutations go through ","type":"text"},{"code":"inout State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which is predictable, snapshottable, and testable. SwiftUI observation needs an ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reference type. Reconciling these two requires a class that mirrors the struct.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" generates that class for you ("},{"code":"<StructName>Observer","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") and wires up the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance that bridges the two. Don’t hand-write the observer. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pack → reduce → unpack-diff → observe"},{"type":"text","text":" cycle is what gives you per-property re-renders without coupling reducers to a class."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Slice","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" extends this to nested struct slices: each slice gets its own observer class so observation stays granular even across composition.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"2. Reducers are pure and synchronous","anchor":"2-Reducers-are-pure-and-synchronous"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Reducers take ","type":"text"},{"code":"inout State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and an "},{"code":"Action","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", mutate state in place, and return an optional "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". They never "},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", never "},{"code":"throw","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and never call I\/O directly."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Why: pure synchronous mutations are trivially testable, deterministic, and snapshot-friendly. When you need async work (network, disk, timers), return an effect — a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":" async closure that runs off the MainActor and dispatches follow-up actions back through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"send"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"3. Effects run off MainActor; sends hop back","anchor":"3-Effects-run-off-MainActor-sends-hop-back"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","isActive":true},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Sendable (Send) async -> Void","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" runs effects in ","type":"text"},{"code":"Task { @concurrent in }","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" so they don’t block UI. "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Send","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"@MainActor @Sendable (Action) -> Void","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so dispatching from inside an effect always lands back on MainActor — no manual hops, no race conditions on state.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The split is deliberate: effects own the work, the reducer owns the state."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"4. Persistence is invisible","anchor":"4-Persistence-is-invisible"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reducers mutate "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"text":" properties; ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" records every change in a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet","type":"reference"},{"text":"; ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true},{"text":" debounces and drains those changesets through ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" closures."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You never write ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"db.save()"},{"text":" in a feature. A reducer that adds an item is identical whether the entity is persisted to SwiftData, SQLite, or nowhere — register or don’t register a writer. This is the principle that makes Swidux apps feel small: persistence stops being a concern of feature code.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"5. Synchronous state, async persistence","anchor":"5-Synchronous-state-async-persistence"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State updates synchronously inside the reducer for instant UI feedback. Persistence happens asynchronously: "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"text":" change tracking is in-memory and free; the debounced persistence flush coalesces rapid mutations into a single batched write.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Tap-tap-tap-tap on an increment button updates the UI on every tap and produces one DB write a moment later. Reducers stay synchronous; storage stays cheap.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"6. Plugins are the single extension point","anchor":"6-Plugins-are-the-single-extension-point"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Everything that hangs off the dispatch cycle is a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","isActive":true},{"text":". Persistence, undo, killswitch, parental gate, paywall — same protocol, same lifecycle hooks. You can add your own without forking Swidux.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Two structural patterns:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Core middleware","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":") — action-agnostic. Doesn’t know your action type. Couples only to state shape ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" for undo; "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" keypaths for persistence)."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Domain plugins","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KillswitchPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ParentalGatePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":", your own) — owns a state slice and an action enum. Wires into your root types via keypath + action lifter + extractor."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The decision rule: ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"does this need to know your action type?"}]},{"text":" If no, write core middleware and use ","type":"text"},{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". If yes, write a domain plugin and use ","type":"text"},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"7. Bind to the store, not to `@State`","anchor":"7-Bind-to-the-store-not-to-State"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Form inputs read from the store and dispatch on write. Use ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/binding(_:sending:)","isActive":true},{"text":" for the common case (read one property, dispatch one action), and fall back to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Binding(get:set:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when the read is a transformation (optional unwraps, derived values) or the setter wraps the dispatch in animation or branching. Don’t buffer mutable form state in ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and write back on a button.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Why: every mutation flows through the reducer, which means undo\/redo, persistence, and any plugin that watches the dispatch cycle sees every keystroke (subject to coalescing). If you stash state in ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", those plugins are blind to it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The trade-off is more dispatches per keystroke. Coalescing — see ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"text":" — collapses bursts of the same action into a single undo step.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"8. Registration order matters at the boundaries","anchor":"8-Registration-order-matters-at-the-boundaries"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"text":" snapshots in ","type":"text"},{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so it must run ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}]},{"text":" any plugin or reducer mutates state — register it first. ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true},{"text":" drains changelogs in ","type":"text"},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so it wants the post-mutation state — register it after undo. Domain plugins use only ","type":"text"},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so their relative order rarely matters.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The recommended order:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. snapshots first","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. drains after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. domain plugins","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)","plugins.register(parentalGatePlugin)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"9. Strict concurrency, on purpose","anchor":"9-Strict-concurrency-on-purpose"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux is built for ","type":"text"},{"code":"swiftLanguageMode(.v6)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and assumes Swift 6 strict concurrency throughout. State must be ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The macros mark generated code carefully. Effects use explicit isolation (","type":"text"},{"code":"@Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"@MainActor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"@concurrent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This is friction at first — you’ll get warnings about ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" types. Honour them. The result is a state-management layer that composes safely with ","type":"text"},{"code":"async\/await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and SwiftData without the surprise data races you get from pre-Swift 6 designs.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"10. The store is opinionated; your app is not","anchor":"10-The-store-is-opinionated-your-app-is-not"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux gives you a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a reducer protocol, a plugin protocol, and three optional plugins. It does not give you:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A dependency-injection container (write your own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppEnvironment"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A navigation library (use SwiftUI navigation)."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A network layer (use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession"},{"type":"text","text":", structured concurrency, or whatever you want)."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An opinion on database (SwiftData, GRDB, SQLite, Core Data — register a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StateWriter"},{"type":"text","text":" and Swidux doesn’t care)."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The store owns one job: take an action, produce a new state, run effects. Everything else is yours.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Anti-patterns","anchor":"Anti-patterns"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"try"},{"type":"text","text":" inside a reducer — return an effect instead."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Hand-writing the observer class when you could use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Calling "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"db.save()"},{"type":"text","text":" from inside a reducer — use "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Mutating state from inside an effect — effects dispatch actions; the reducer mutates."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Owning the store with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@StateObject"},{"type":"text","text":" — use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":", not "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ObservableObject"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Buffering form state in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" and committing on submit — bind to the store directly."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Registering "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" before "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" — snapshot must precede mutation."}]}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","title":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Coalescing persistence plugin."}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxPlugin":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxplugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","abstract":[{"text":"A plugin that participates in the Swidux dispatch cycle.","type":"text"}],"title":"SwiduxPlugin","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxPlugin"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","title":"Swidux"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Effect":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Effect"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/effect","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An async unit of work returned by a reducer."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","title":"Effect","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Effect"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ArchitectureGuide":{"type":"topic","role":"article","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","title":"Architecture & Performance","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide","abstract":[{"text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginArchitecture":{"type":"topic","role":"article","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","title":"Plugin Architecture","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture","abstract":[{"text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","title":"UndoPlugin","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityStore"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every mutation for downstream persistence."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","title":"EntityStore","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityStore"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ChangeSet":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ChangeSet","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ChangeSet"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/changeset","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tracks which entity IDs have been created\/updated or deleted."}],"title":"ChangeSet"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Send":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Send"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/send","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A function for dispatching actions back to the store from within an effect."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Send","title":"Send","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Send"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/StateWriter":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"StateWriter"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/statewriter","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Accumulates entity snapshots and produces batched async persistence work."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter","title":"StateWriter","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"StateWriter"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store/binding(_:sending:)":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"binding"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s7KeyPathC","text":"KeyPath"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"State"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux0A10ObservableP8ObserverQa","text":"Observer"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":">, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"sending"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Action"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI7BindingV","text":"Binding"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}]},"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store\/binding(_:sending:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a SwiftUI "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Binding"},{"type":"text","text":" that reads a property through the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"observer tree and dispatches an action when written."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/binding(_:sending:)","title":"binding(_:sending:)"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingYourFirstApp":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingyourfirstapp","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build a counter app from scratch and meet the four moving parts of a Swidux project: state, action, reducer, and store."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingYourFirstApp","title":"Build Your First Swidux App"}}}